Feature: The forest and the lanes
  The field of Towers is a valley with a forest. The forest covers all the field, except for
  the [[lane]]s, the [[clearing]]s and the lake. The trees are 20 m to 30 m tall. Three lanes go
  from each home tower to the home tower of the other team: the west lane through the west
  tower, the mid lane through the centre tower, and the east lane through the east tower. The
  lake is between the Blue home tower and the west tower. The west lane goes along its shore.

  The trees hide a drone that flies [[low]], below the treetops. A team sees a low drone only
  along a line that has no trees on it: along a lane, across a clearing or across the lake. A
  drone above the trees is seen over the forest, as far as the team sees. A tower, or a drone
  above the trees, also looks down on a low drone that is within 75 m. Thus a drone that flies
  low can get near the enemy and not be seen.

  Expectation: The trees hide a drone that flies low
    Given the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    And the Red scout is low in the east lane, near the first Blue drone
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is unknown

  Expectation: A drone above the trees is seen over the forest
    Given the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    And the Red scout is high over the east lane, near the first Blue drone
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is seen

  Expectation: A team sees a low drone along the lane
    Given the first Blue drone is low in the mid lane
    And the Red scout is low in the mid lane, ahead of the first Blue drone
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is seen

  Expectation: A team sees a low drone across the lake
    Given the first Blue drone is low in the west lane, on the shore of the lake
    And the Red scout is low over the lake
    When the game runs for 10 seconds
    Then the Red scout on the Blue map is seen

Feature: Flying low
  Each order is flown high or [[low]]. A drone that flies high goes straight to where it is
  sent, over the forest. A drone that flies low goes along the lanes, below the treetops. At
  the end it circles low if it is in a [[clearing]]. In a lane or over the forest there is no
  space to circle, so there it climbs above the trees and circles high.

  Expectation: A drone that flies high goes straight over the forest
    Given the first Blue drone is at the Blue home tower
    When the first Blue drone is sent high to the west tower
    Then the way of the first Blue drone is straight over the forest
    And the orbit of the first Blue drone is high

  Expectation: A drone that flies low goes along the lanes
    Given the first Blue drone is at the Blue home tower
    When the first Blue drone is sent low to the west tower
    Then the way of the first Blue drone is along the west lane
    And the orbit of the first Blue drone is low

  Expectation: A drone that flies low to the forest climbs to circle
    Given the first Blue drone is at the Blue home tower
    When the first Blue drone is sent low to a point in the forest
    Then the way of the first Blue drone is along the mid lane
    And the orbit of the first Blue drone is high
